4
00:00:09,760 --> 00:00:10,080
That's right.

5
00:00:10,300 --> 00:00:13,860
Today we're going to take a look at our favorite maybe kind of food.

6
00:00:14,400 --> 00:00:20,100
We're taking a look at the fast food, all these yummy but not very healthy types of food.

7
00:00:20,760 --> 00:00:21,200
Yeah, we are.

8
00:00:21,360 --> 00:00:28,080
So let's listen to our dialogue and when we come back we'll be talking about what some of these foods are and what some of the phrases you've heard mean.

9
00:00:34,570 --> 00:00:35,210
I'm hungry.

10
00:00:35,510 --> 00:00:36,730
Let's order up something to eat.

11
00:00:37,130 --> 00:00:37,570
Okay.

12
00:00:37,890 --> 00:00:41,170
Maybe we can order a soup and a salad from the restaurant down the street.

13
00:00:41,430 --> 00:00:44,910
I was thinking of getting a hamburger, fries and a chocolate sundae.

14
00:00:45,250 --> 00:00:46,790
You eat too much junk food.

15
00:00:47,230 --> 00:00:50,250
That sort of stuff clogs up your arteries and is very high in cholesterol.

16
00:00:51,240 --> 00:00:52,890
Well I never seem to gain weight so I don't mind.

17
00:00:53,480 --> 00:00:56,050
It's not only about getting fat or not, it's about being healthy.

18
00:00:57,180 --> 00:00:59,090
You could really have some health problems later on.

19
00:00:59,710 --> 00:01:02,230
How about pizza or maybe some fried chicken?

20
00:01:02,690 --> 00:01:04,310
Better yet, let's order some hot dogs.

21
00:01:04,870 --> 00:01:05,890
You're a lost cause.

22
00:01:07,320 --> 00:01:10,440
All right, we're back.

23
00:01:10,440 --> 00:01:15,400
So now let's take a look at language takeaway.

24
00:01:15,400 --> 00:01:15,890
Language takeaway.

25
00:01:17,820 --> 00:01:21,410
So first up on language takeaway is a very unhealthy food.

26
00:01:21,680 --> 00:01:23,190
It's called a chocolate sundae.

27
00:01:23,430 --> 00:01:23,850
That's right.

28
00:01:24,030 --> 00:01:27,490
We wanted to order hamburger, french fries and a chocolate sundae.

29
00:01:27,680 --> 00:01:32,280
So chocolate we know that this is the flavor that comes from cocoa.

30
00:01:32,280 --> 00:01:33,670
But what is a sundae?

31
00:01:34,150 --> 00:01:37,790
Well basically a sundae is a kind of ice cream dessert.

32
00:01:38,680 --> 00:01:49,360
It comes in a cup or a bowl and it's usually vanilla ice cream with chocolate sauce and then oftentimes a cherry on top.

33
00:01:49,390 --> 00:01:57,070
So as you can see the word is pronounced exactly like the day, sundae, but it has a different spelling in the end.

34
00:01:58,000 --> 00:02:01,400
S-U-N-D-A-E, sundae.

35
00:02:01,400 --> 00:02:02,940
So this is a chocolate sundae.

36
00:02:02,940 --> 00:02:06,830
So when you see this spelling, a sundae with an E, that's the dessert.

37
00:02:07,210 --> 00:02:08,750
If you see it with a Y, that's the day.

38
00:02:09,560 --> 00:02:10,560
Exactly.

39
00:02:10,560 --> 00:02:14,360
So chocolate sundae, actually a very delicious dessert, but remember it's ice cream.

40
00:02:14,360 --> 00:02:14,520
That's right.

41
00:02:15,360 --> 00:02:21,040
And all of these types of food, hamburger, chocolate sundae, it's called junk food.

42
00:02:21,040 --> 00:02:21,300
Junk food.

43
00:02:22,040 --> 00:02:23,040
Well food you know.

44
00:02:23,040 --> 00:02:24,040
Junk.

45
00:02:24,040 --> 00:02:25,440
What is an example of junk, Marco?

46
00:02:26,040 --> 00:02:28,280
Well something that's not good or useful anymore.

47
00:02:28,640 --> 00:02:32,700
So maybe you have trash that you need to get rid of, like an old TV.

48
00:02:33,140 --> 00:02:33,640
That's junk.

49
00:02:34,400 --> 00:02:37,380
So my mom would always say, throw away this junk.

50
00:02:37,840 --> 00:02:39,240
It's stuff that you don't need.

51
00:02:39,560 --> 00:02:41,260
So junk is things that you would throw away.

52
00:02:41,860 --> 00:02:44,080
Junk food is the kind of food that's not healthy for you.

53
00:02:44,200 --> 00:02:48,060
It's the food that you shouldn't eat, but it tends to be really delicious.

54
00:02:48,460 --> 00:02:49,000
That's right.

55
00:02:49,660 --> 00:02:57,980
So for example, the hamburger, french fries, a chocolate sundae, all this would fall under this category of junk food.

56
00:02:58,220 --> 00:02:58,620
That's right.

57
00:02:59,520 --> 00:03:02,800
And one of the things about junk food is that it's high in cholesterol.

58
00:03:02,800 --> 00:03:04,020
Now what is cholesterol, Marco?

59
00:03:04,340 --> 00:03:04,860
That's right.

60
00:03:05,760 --> 00:03:06,760
So you always have to be careful.

61
00:03:06,760 --> 00:03:11,300
Your doctor says that you shouldn't have or you have to be careful about having high cholesterol.

62
00:03:12,120 --> 00:03:18,220
And that's just basically, it's a type of fat that is found in animal products.

63
00:03:18,680 --> 00:03:25,560
So for example, beef has cholesterol and it's dangerous because it could maybe cause health problems.

64
00:03:25,560 --> 00:03:25,700
That's right.

65
00:03:26,560 --> 00:03:36,240
So my friend needed to lower his cholesterol and his doctor told him he should eat less red meat, eat more vegetables and fruits instead.

66
00:03:36,880 --> 00:03:37,140
That's right.

67
00:03:37,880 --> 00:03:41,180
So cholesterol is a, you'll see it all the time when you're shopping.

68
00:03:41,560 --> 00:03:46,450
You'll see that it's low in cholesterol or no sugar or no calories, stuff like that.

69
00:03:47,040 --> 00:03:48,040
Exactly.

70
00:03:48,040 --> 00:03:53,870
Now, a food that is very, very high in cholesterol is fried chicken, but it's also very delicious.

71
00:03:54,480 --> 00:03:54,650
That's right.

72
00:03:55,480 --> 00:03:56,480
Fried chicken.

73
00:03:56,480 --> 00:04:03,680
Now as you see, the first word there is fried and that means that it was cooked in hot oil.

74
00:04:04,540 --> 00:04:04,680
That's right.

75
00:04:05,540 --> 00:04:18,000
And what's important to remember about most American fried chicken is that the chicken is usually put in a batter, so like a milk, egg, flour sauce, and then it's fried.

76
00:04:18,000 --> 00:04:21,700
So on the outside it's very, very crispy and salty.

77
00:04:21,700 --> 00:04:21,840
That's right.

78
00:04:22,700 --> 00:04:27,480
So it's covered in like a type of bread, like a crispy bread.

79
00:04:27,480 --> 00:04:28,110
Yeah, that's right.

80
00:04:29,520 --> 00:04:33,550
It's usually very greasy, so when you eat it, you have lots of grease on your fingers.

81
00:04:34,440 --> 00:04:38,810
But one of the reasons it tastes so good is because as you say, Marco, it's fried in oil.

82
00:04:39,630 --> 00:04:40,050
That's right.

83
00:04:40,570 --> 00:04:41,270
Very good.

84
