100
00:05:35,320 --> 00:05:43,130
So one of the first phrases is actually something that I'm excited to talk about because it comes up a lot in directions when we're giving people directions somewhere.

101
00:05:43,560 --> 00:05:50,430
So one of the people in the dialogue said, we can order a soup and salad from the restaurant down the street.

102
00:05:50,770 --> 00:05:50,990
Right.

103
00:05:51,490 --> 00:05:55,450
So this is, you're basically telling the person where the restaurant is.

104
00:05:55,830 --> 00:05:59,720
And when you say something is down the street, it means that it's nearby.

105
00:06:00,420 --> 00:06:00,800
It is.

106
00:06:00,900 --> 00:06:01,200
It's nearby.

107
00:06:02,600 --> 00:06:08,320
It's on the same street or it's just a few minutes walk from where you are now.

108
00:06:08,720 --> 00:06:09,000
Right, right.

109
00:06:09,720 --> 00:06:13,640
So you can say, my apartment is just down the street from this park.

110
00:06:14,280 --> 00:06:14,900
So it's very close.

111
00:06:15,320 --> 00:06:16,940
Or you could say, I know him.

112
00:06:17,440 --> 00:06:20,580
He lived down the street from me when we were children.

113
00:06:20,880 --> 00:06:24,160
Okay, so he lived really, really close to you.

114
00:06:24,160 --> 00:06:24,310
Very good.

115
00:06:25,160 --> 00:06:34,610
Now, when we were talking about junk food and we were talking about how it's not healthy, we said that junk food clogs up your arteries.

116
00:06:35,150 --> 00:06:35,590
All right.

117
00:06:36,080 --> 00:06:39,050
A couple important words here to clog up arteries.

118
00:06:39,750 --> 00:06:42,270
The verb to clog, what does that mean?

119
00:06:42,590 --> 00:06:48,410
Clog with a G. It means it gets in the way or obstructs it.

120
00:06:48,910 --> 00:06:49,250
All right.

121
00:06:49,550 --> 00:06:56,660
So for example, if a drain, in my sink, if a drain is clogged, the water does not go down.

122
00:06:57,440 --> 00:06:58,440
Right.

123
00:06:58,440 --> 00:06:59,840
So the water starts to build and build and build.

124
00:06:59,840 --> 00:07:04,300
Actually, it's very dangerous because if it comes up too much, the water will go on the floor.

125
00:07:05,640 --> 00:07:07,600
But that's a drain, that's a sink.

126
00:07:07,600 --> 00:07:12,760
If you're talking about the heart, you would say that cholesterol clogs up your arteries.

127
00:07:13,460 --> 00:07:13,600
Right.

128
00:07:13,760 --> 00:07:17,800
So your arteries are like these tubes where blood passes.

129
00:07:17,800 --> 00:07:20,760
And of course, if they're clogged up, then blood can't pass.

130
00:07:21,520 --> 00:07:22,520
That's right.

131
00:07:22,520 --> 00:07:32,820
And if it's very serious, people sometimes have to have heart surgery to clear those arteries to take the blockage, the clogging away from the arteries.

132
00:07:33,360 --> 00:07:33,580
That's right.

133
00:07:34,360 --> 00:07:35,360
That's right.

134
00:07:35,360 --> 00:07:36,360
Okay.

135
00:07:36,360 --> 00:07:39,840
So that is to clog something up or something is clogged up.

136
00:07:39,840 --> 00:07:46,640
